SOURCE CHECK: I read the cached page text, src/gr-qc_9812032.cached.txt, myself. In (3.2) the leading factor shows as '1' over '2' with a blank, and in (2.12) as '1' over a blank denominator. In (3.3) the pi is dropped from 'pi^{n/2}', and on the same line as (3.2) '(2)^n' stands for (2 pi)^n. This is a consistent pattern of lost pi glyphs. The tree's '-(1/2)' quotation is that loss. The '9/64' on p.7 has no pi and is legible. This confirms the audit's discrepancy: the tree quotes (3.2) with 1/2 (fewsterteo.py:29-30, 465), while the printed factor is 1/(2 pi). It is a transcription loss and not an error in the paper.

VACUITY GUARD: my script verify/rederive/ft32_vacuity.py gives 13/13 PASS. Every mutation breaks the printed numbers:
- leading factor A = 1/2 gives 9 pi/64; A = 1/pi gives 9/32; A = 1/(4 pi) gives 9/128;
- the transform of f in place of f^{1/2} gives a non-rational, dimensionful ratio;
